{
  /*
   * The third config, and it exists because the two above it left the gate
   * suite itself typechecked by NOTHING.
   *
   * `scripts/` is ~274KB of TypeScript, and it includes `check.ts` — the one
   * thing standing between this repository and a bad deploy — plus
   * `auth-e2e.ts`, which drives the real browser auth modules against the real
   * Worker. Both are bundled by esbuild at the point of use, and **esbuild
   * strips types without checking them**, so every one of them compiled
   * whatever it said.
   *
   * They could not simply be added to `tsconfig.json`'s `include`. These are
   * Node programs: they need `@types/node`, which the app config deliberately
   * does not carry, and the app's `lib` set has no `process`. They also import
   * from `src/`, which is why `DOM` is here as well — `check.ts` drives the
   * canvas effects through a recording context, so it needs both halves.
   *
   * `noUnusedLocals` / `noUnusedParameters` are deliberately OFF here, unlike
   * the other two configs. A gate that measures a quantity and then asserts on
   * a different one is a real defect this project has shipped before, but it is
   * caught by reading the gate, not by the compiler — whereas a probe variable
   * kept deliberately beside the assertion it documents is normal in this file
   * and should not fail the build.
   *
   * **KNOWN HOLE, and it is in this config rather than in the code it checks:
   * the global `Buffer` is `any` here.** `@cloudflare/workers-types` declares
   * `declare const Buffer: any` in the global scope, and that clobbers
   * `@types/node`'s. Both have to be in scope — `check.ts` imports from `src/`
   * (DOM) and from `worker/` (workers-types) in the same file — so anything in
   * `scripts/` that touches the global `Buffer` is unchecked, and it fails in a
   * confusing direction: the *interface* is lost rather than the inference, so
   * annotating a binding as `Buffer` does not recover it and the value falls
   * back to `Uint8Array`'s no-argument `toString`. Reduced to a one-line `.d.ts`
   * repro on 2026-09-15. Prefer `Uint8Array` and explicit decoding in new
   * `scripts/` code; do not read a `Buffer`-typed expression here and assume the
   * compiler checked it.
   *
   * Requiring the DOM/workers-types pair is also why five `as BufferSource`
   * casts exist in `worker/totp.ts` and `worker/accounts.ts` — DOM declares the
   * stricter of two `BufferSource` definitions and wins. That file carries the
   * argument.
   */
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "types": ["node", "@cloudflare/workers-types"],
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "moduleDetection": "force",
    "noEmit": true,
    "strict": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true
  },
  "include": ["scripts/**/*.ts"]
}
